  "key_evidence": [
    "Why it matters: Lisbon's published 60.9 was a starting value. This is the first time it has been measured against evidence.",
    "A city-owned company ran the Glória funicular with a cable not certified for passengers. The crash on 3 September 2025 killed 16 people.",
    "Compensation has been slow. By late August 2026 the insurer had made four compensation payments; in June, 38 victims or families were still waiting. The dead brake operator's children still had no school grant in March 2026.",
    "Lisbon is credited for counting its homeless population each year and for a 2024-2030 homeless plan. The count fell from 3,378 to 3,122.",
    "Lisbon measures 35.0 of 100 (Developing). A downgrade from 60.9 is proposed, with low confidence."
  ],
